# Verifies: SPEC §3.6 (generics) / D-FUNC-05 using an operator on an unconstrained type
# parameter / D-DIAG-02 E1013
# With no traits/inheritance, no constraint syntax exists for type parameters. A
# function body cannot directly use `<` (an operator defined only for specific concrete
# types) against an unconstrained T; this is caught by the generic-body-level check as E1013.
# (`==`/`!=` are always applicable to T as structural equality, D-OP-06)

def smaller[T](a: T, b: T): T
    if a < b
        return a
    else
        return b

print(smaller(1, 2))
